      "problem": "Given the arithmetic sequence $f(n)=2n-5$ for $n\\ge 1,$what is the index of the term $41?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $f(n)=41$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =2n-5 \\\\ 41 & =2n-5 \\\\ 46 & =2n \\\\ n & =23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $41$ is the $23$rd term of the sequence.",
